+# Thermodynamic star creator cold review
+
+**PASS under the declared uniform full-active impurity inequality**, source89fc2322090be9808f6ccc57bf6ceafcf6b7027387aa154332824fabe612f087. Complete proof read, no numerical execution. Reuses the independently reviewed quasi-local creator/filter and Gaussian extraction lemmas explicitly.
+
+The common-algebra construction correctly identifies fixed centered boxes only. Wrap bonds need not embed into the infinite interaction; their contribution to fixed-time local evolution vanishes by the hopping-path tail. Compact-time convergence plus integrable filter tails establishes the local-approximant limit without an invalid global finite-torus norm embedding. The same uniformly quasi-local tail controls subsequent limits.
+
+Bounded covariance projectors are Riemann integrable away from finitely many nodes. Removing fixed node neighborhoods before taking the grid limit controls their density uniformly, so local covariance and Wick expectations converge. The almost-everywhere projector property yields the pure quasifree state; purity is not inferred from convergence of arbitrary pure finite states or a uniform gap.
+
+The intrinsic coefficient c_j=omega({gamma_j,Y})/2 has the uniform rapid tail because odd ball approximants anticommute with remote Majoranas. Fixed-j convergence and a common summable weighted tail justify every fixed weighted-l1 limit. Centered torus graph distance and coordinate distance are uniformly comparable, so zero-extension does not spoil the bound. Fourier derivatives follow from weighted-l1 convergence. The smooth object is the unprojected cell/Majorana coefficient symbol: neither individual band eigenvectors nor the direction-dependent positive-frequency projector becomes smooth at nodes. This distinction is essential and correctly retained.
+
+The GNS step is valid on the full active representation provided the assumed finite inequality holds in both active parities relative to the SAME E0. Local polynomials create finitely many quasiparticles. Bounded one-particle excitation dispersion makes those vectors analytic for H; density of local projected one-particle functions supplies a dense core. B_A is bounded self-adjoint, preserving the core property. Since [H_L,X] is a fixed local polynomial for local X, state convergence passes the finite quadratic-form lower bound to that core and then to the self-adjoint form domain. Thus H+B_A>=delta survives although H itself is gapless. This proves existence and boundedness of the impurity inverses in this GNS representation, and the filter/cocycle identity gives the exact double inverse on Omega.
+
+No interchange of small-U and volume limits occurs. The result does not transfer finite-L6 positive higher-particle weight, determine node vanishing, or construct an interacting ground state. Constants remain conditional on fixed hopping/kappa and the same uniform full-active stiffness premise. No blocker found in the stated scope.
